{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:5760f6e1476e1430","name":"The Tommaba Brotherhood","source":{"id":"source:reference-5760f6e1476e1430","title":"The Tommaba Brotherhood","revision":23394,"timestamp":"2024-09-25T16:33:07Z","sha256":"daf35052907cf2f36067b2d43f70761a4098bc8f79fcbda83bb138ede248f981","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=23394","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20Tommaba%20Brotherhood&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-5760f6e1476e1430","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Few independent scout organizations exist, but one was born out of a large tragedy. The Tommaba Brotherhood is a loose affiliation of scouts who are natives of the destroyed planet ",{"tag":"a","children":["Alderaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Alderaan","referenceId":"reference:c7a6b713a1619ee9"},". Many of those who called ",{"tag":"a","children":["Alderaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Alderaan","referenceId":"reference:c7a6b713a1619ee9"}," home settle on ",{"tag":"a","children":["New Alderaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/New_Alderaan?action=edit&redlink=1"},", but others wander the galaxy without a home. Many of these wanderers end up as independent scouts who band together in a loose, informal affiliation. Their name comes from a herd animal that wandered the plains of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Alderaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Alderaan","referenceId":"reference:c7a6b713a1619ee9"},". Despite the masculine name, both males and females can be members, as long as they are from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Alderaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Alderaan","referenceId":"reference:c7a6b713a1619ee9"},". \n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
